window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_b1-f5d7c768bb870561"]={"key":"ny_b1-f5d7c768bb870561","group":"ny_b1","uid":"f5d7c768bb870561","rank":86,"title":"silverbrook kinship iep advocacy brief","occupation":"child_family_school_social_workers","archetype":"authored_doc","subbatch":"corpus_b1","prompt":"You are Ana Macaulay, the child and family social worker supporting Silverbrook Board’s family-services unit. Noor Aubert, a grandmother caring for a child in a new kinship placement, will attend the child’s IEP meeting on Thursday without a professional beside her. The underlying case material is a 118-page CCWIS export, three provider reports, and a school attendance ledger, but none of those materials is being sent with this assignment and Noor cannot manage a case summary in the room. The only case facts cleared for the brief are that the child has experienced two prior placement moves, continuity of instruction was interrupted around those moves, there is a widening reading gap, and older diagnostic wording remains in the file but is not a useful way to lead this meeting. The school team is likely to treat placement history as outside its lane, even though leaving it out entirely would obscure the educational context. Noor needs both an immediate plan for reading access and a clean account of what the team is deciding, and a one-page handout cannot give those aims equal billing, so make the brief’s priority unmistakable. There is also a difficult line between what the team must address or document and what Noor should press for based on the information available; do not turn a requested support into a promised entitlement. Prepare `noor_aubert_iep_advocacy_brief.docx` as a polished, editable, one-page brief Noor can hold and speak from in the meeting. It should use plain, respectful language, give her usable words and questions rather than professional commentary, and leave enough visual room for short notes. Keep the focus on Thursday’s educational decisions, include only the limited case facts above, do not name or infer a diagnosis, do not invent scores, dates, service minutes, attendance totals, legal status, or prior school responses, and do not burden Noor with citations or agency process. Have it ready for Estelle Wolstenholme by 3:00 p.m. Wednesday. Write the file into the top level of the working directory using exactly the filename given.\n\n---\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `noor_aubert_iep_advocacy_brief.docx` — A one-page, plain-language IEP advocacy brief that Noor Aubert can speak from and annotate during the meeting. (Exactly one editable DOCX file; No more than one rendered page; Written directly for Noor Aubert to use in the meeting; Includes usable speaking language, questions, and room for short notes; Uses only the case facts stated in the request; Does not name or infer a diagnosis or invent scores, dates, service minutes, attendance totals, legal status, or prior school responses; Contains no legal citations or agency-process instructions; Must be saved at the top level of the working directory as noor_aubert_iep_advocacy_brief.docx)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/noor_aubert_iep_advocacy_brief.docx","bytes":39924,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/5366fe652ada6cc7f3d2d460f0bab236a4088ca71e7419b2127c84fed9276373.docx","sha256":"5366fe652ada6cc7f3d2d460f0bab236a4088ca71e7419b2127c84fed9276373","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"NOOR AUBERT  |  THURSDAY IEP MEETING\nA reading plan I can understand, use, and check\nKeep the meeting on current learning. I can ask for clear decisions without assuming the answer.\nOPEN WITH (say this)\n“I’m Noor, the child’s grandmother and kinship caregiver. I’m here to understand the reading need and leave with a workable plan for learning and follow-up.”\nPRIMARY — LEAVE WITH A READING PLAN\nCurrent need → measurable goal → targeted instruction → how we will check progress.\nALSO SECURE\nA plain record of decisions, reasons, owners, and timing.\n1  MAKE THE READING NEED PLAIN\n“What can the child do in reading now, and where is it hard?”\n“Which part are we talking about—decoding words, reading smoothly, understanding, or showing an answer in writing?”\n“What assessment, work sample, observation, or progress data supports that description? When was it collected?”\n“How did the team consider interrupted instruction or school changes when reading this information?”\n“What reading instruction or intervention has been provided, and what observable progress followed?”\n“If the information is not enough, what further review or assessment will the team consider?”\nContext I can add (briefly)\n“There were two prior placement moves, and instruction was interrupted around those moves. I’m sharing this only as context for educational access and for interpreting today’s data—not as proof of a diagnosis or cause.”\nIf old wording comes up\n“I’d like us to use current reading evidence and needs; older wording alone does not tell us what support is needed now.”\nAttendance\n“What attendance information is relevant to interpreting this data, and what context should we keep in mind?” (Information to examine, not an assumed explanation.)\n2  ASK FOR AN IMPLEMENTABLE PLAN\n“What measurable reading goal fits the established baseline? How will progress be measured, how often checked, and how/when will it be shared with me?”\n“What targeted or specialized reading instruction is proposed? How is it different from an access accommodation?”\n“If a service is agreed, what is the frequency/schedule, who is responsible, and where will it happen? Please avoid ‘as needed.’”\n“What can begin now under the current or agreed plan, while any further review is considered?”\n“How will instruction, materials, and communication stay continuous after placement changes?”\n“Who is my point of contact, and what follow-up/review date should we put on the record?”\nMY ROLE (clarify, don’t assume)\n“I want my observations considered. Please tell me who is recognized to consent, sign, or receive formal notices. I will ask what a signature represents before signing.”\nREQUESTS ≠ GUARANTEES\nI can ask the team to consider supports; the team’s decision is not predetermined. If a request is declined, I can ask: “What is the reason and what information supports that decision?”\nQUICK NOTES — write the answer, owner, and timing\nReading goal / evidence: ________________________________________________\nSupport details (who • how often • where): _________________________________\nDecision or open item + reason: ___________________________________________\nContact + follow-up date: _________________________________________________\nCLOSE WITH (read back)\n“Let me read back what we decided: what starts now, how progress will be checked and shared, who does what, and by when. Please note any proposal declined or left open, with the reason. May I have the resulting plan or meeting record to review?”","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"R01","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The required file exists under the exact filename and is a valid, editable DOCX rather than a renamed image or PDF.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Submitted deliverable and DOCX package structure.","grader_hint":"Confirm `noor_aubert_iep_advocacy_brief.docx` is at the submission root, opens successfully, and contains editable document content."},{"rubric_item_id":"R02","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The complete brief renders on one page without clipped, hidden, or overflowing content.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Rendered DOCX.","grader_hint":"Render using a standard office engine and verify that all substantive content, including footer content, remains on a single page."},{"rubric_item_id":"R03","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The page has a clear visual hierarchy that Noor can scan while participating in a live meeting.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Overall page organization and typography.","grader_hint":"Look for distinct, concise blocks, readable type, and obvious navigation rather than a dense memo or uninterrupted wall of text."},{"rubric_item_id":"R04","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The brief provides practical writable space for several short meeting notes.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered page.","grader_hint":"Confirm there are visible blank lines, cells, or equivalent spaces that could accept at least three short handwritten notes without covering printed text."},{"rubric_item_id":"R05","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document is written to Noor as the person speaking, not as a case note about her or a briefing for professionals.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Voice and wording throughout the brief.","grader_hint":"Award when the page consistently uses first-person scripts or direct second-person prompts that Noor can use aloud."},{"rubric_item_id":"R06","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The brief makes one primary meeting priority unmistakable while still preserving the secondary concern.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Opening, ordering, emphasis, and closing of the brief.","grader_hint":"Accept either a reading-plan-first framing or a decision-record-first framing if one is deliberately dominant and the other is still addressed."},{"rubric_item_id":"R07","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The brief gives Noor a concise opening statement identifying herself as the child's grandmother or kinship caregiver.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Opening speaking script.","grader_hint":"Look for language Noor can say aloud that accurately identifies her relationship without claiming an unverified legal role."},{"rubric_item_id":"R08","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The opening script states a constructive purpose centered on the child's learning and a workable plan for the meeting.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Opening speaking script.","grader_hint":"The purpose should orient the team toward educational needs and decisions rather than blame, diagnosis, or a review of the whole case."},{"rubric_item_id":"R09","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The brief accurately mentions two prior placement moves.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Case-context language.","grader_hint":"Accept equivalent wording that clearly preserves the number two and describes placement changes."},{"rubric_item_id":"R10","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Placement history is connected narrowly to interrupted continuity of instruction and the educational context for the reading gap.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Case-context script.","grader_hint":"Award when the page explains why the moves are relevant to learning without turning the meeting into a child-welfare history review."},{"rubric_item_id":"R11","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The brief explicitly avoids presenting the placement moves as proof that they caused a disability or diagnosis.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Calibrated causal wording.","grader_hint":"Look for language such as educational context, interrupted opportunity, or a factor to consider, rather than a definitive clinical or causal conclusion."},{"rubric_item_id":"R12","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The brief demonstrates when the usual instinct to leave placement history out of a school meeting stops being useful.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scope and framing of the historical statement.","grader_hint":"Award when history is included only to explain current educational access, continuity, or data interpretation and is not expanded into irrelevant case detail."},{"rubric_item_id":"R13","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The current concern is described as a reading gap or reading need.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Opening or issue statement.","grader_hint":"The page should clearly name reading as the educational area requiring attention."},{"rubric_item_id":"R14","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The brief does not name, imply, or invite Noor to argue for a particular diagnosis.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"All clinical, disability, and eligibility language.","grader_hint":"Review the entire page for diagnostic labels, coded hints, or scripts that treat an unspecified diagnosis as established."},{"rubric_item_id":"R15","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Older diagnostic wording is treated as background that does not by itself establish the child's current educational needs, eligibility, or services.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Any treatment of older records or labels.","grader_hint":"Award if the brief either omits the wording entirely or gives Noor a safe way to redirect from old labels to current educational evidence."},{"rubric_item_id":"R16","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The brief prompts Noor to ask for the child's current reading performance in plain language.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Meeting questions.","grader_hint":"Look for a direct question asking what the child can currently do and where the child is having difficulty."},{"rubric_item_id":"R17","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The brief asks the team to distinguish relevant reading components rather than discussing reading as one undifferentiated skill.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Reading questions.","grader_hint":"Accept prompts addressing meaningful components such as decoding, fluency, comprehension, phonological skills, or written response; an exhaustive list is unnecessary."},{"rubric_item_id":"R18","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The brief asks what evidence or data supports the team's description of the current reading need.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Questions about evidence.","grader_hint":"Look for a request to identify the assessment, work sample, observation, or progress data behind the team's account."},{"rubric_item_id":"R19","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The brief asks when the relevant reading information was collected so that stale information is not treated as current.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Questions about data recency.","grader_hint":"Award when Noor is prompted to ask for the date, period, or recency of the evidence."},{"rubric_item_id":"R20","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The brief asks how interrupted instruction or school changes were considered when interpreting performance.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Data-interpretation question.","grader_hint":"Look for a neutral question connecting instructional continuity to interpretation without excusing or diagnosing the reading gap."},{"rubric_item_id":"R21","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Attendance is treated as information to examine rather than an assumed explanation for the reading gap.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Attendance-related wording, if present, and overall reasoning.","grader_hint":"Award when the brief seeks context for attendance and does not state that attendance either caused or disproves the reading need."},{"rubric_item_id":"R22","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The brief does not invent an attendance total, pattern, reason, or characterization.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"All attendance references.","grader_hint":"Confirm that no unsupported number or claim such as chronic absence, refusal, truancy, or move-related clustering appears."},{"rubric_item_id":"R23","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The brief asks what reading instruction or intervention has already been provided.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Meeting questions.","grader_hint":"Look for a direct request to identify prior or current educational responses, without assuming what they were."},{"rubric_item_id":"R24","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The brief asks how the child responded to prior or current instruction using observable progress information.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Intervention-response question.","grader_hint":"The prompt should seek evidence of response or rate of progress, not simply ask whether an intervention was successful."},{"rubric_item_id":"R25","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The brief asks for a measurable reading goal tied to an established baseline if a reading goal is to be included or revised.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Goal-related question or request.","grader_hint":"Award when the page links the goal to current data and a measurable skill or outcome."},{"rubric_item_id":"R26","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The brief does not invent a baseline, grade-equivalent score, target score, or percentage for a reading goal.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"All numerical and goal language.","grader_hint":"Confirm that any target is to be determined from team data rather than supplied by the author."},{"rubric_item_id":"R27","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The brief prompts Noor to ask how progress toward a reading goal will be measured.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Progress-monitoring questions.","grader_hint":"Look for the measurement method or evidence source, not merely a generic promise to monitor."},{"rubric_item_id":"R28","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The brief prompts Noor to ask how often progress will be checked or reviewed.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Progress-monitoring questions.","grader_hint":"Accept a request for an explicit monitoring or review frequency without requiring the brief to invent that frequency."},{"rubric_item_id":"R29","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The brief asks how and when progress information will be communicated to the caregiver.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Reporting question.","grader_hint":"Award when the page seeks a clear reporting method and timing rather than a vague instruction to keep Noor informed."},{"rubric_item_id":"R30","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The brief asks what specialized reading instruction or other targeted educational support the team is proposing.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Support request.","grader_hint":"Look for a question about the actual instructional response, not only accommodations or general encouragement."},{"rubric_item_id":"R31","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The brief distinguishes access accommodations from instruction intended to build reading skills.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Support categories and wording.","grader_hint":"Award when the page makes clear that accommodations may improve access but do not automatically replace skill-focused instruction."},{"rubric_item_id":"R32","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The brief asks the team to identify the frequency or schedule of any agreed targeted service.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Service-detail questions.","grader_hint":"The brief should seek concrete scheduling detail but must not supply invented minutes."},{"rubric_item_id":"R33","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The brief asks who will provide or be responsible for any agreed targeted service.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Service-detail questions.","grader_hint":"Look for responsibility by role or provider type; the brief need not name an individual."},{"rubric_item_id":"R34","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The brief asks where or in what setting any agreed targeted service will occur when that affects implementation.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Service-detail questions.","grader_hint":"Award for a practical prompt about service setting or delivery context."},{"rubric_item_id":"R35","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The brief rejects vague service descriptions such as 'as needed' by prompting for implementable detail.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Service-detail prompts.","grader_hint":"Look for wording that would convert a vague assurance into a specific, recordable commitment."},{"rubric_item_id":"R36","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The brief does not state or imply that a particular intervention, accommodation, service frequency, or placement is guaranteed.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Requests and expected-outcome language.","grader_hint":"Confirm that supports are framed as requests for consideration and decision, not as predetermined entitlements unsupported by the available facts."},{"rubric_item_id":"R37","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The brief accurately conveys that Noor's relevant observations and concerns should be heard and considered by the team.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Participation script.","grader_hint":"Look for language inviting Noor to contribute educationally relevant observations and ask that they be considered."},{"rubric_item_id":"R38","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The brief does not claim that considering Noor's input requires the team to adopt every request she makes.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Participation and decision language.","grader_hint":"Award when the distinction between meaningful participation and guaranteed agreement is maintained."},{"rubric_item_id":"R39","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The brief recognizes that Noor's authority to consent or make educational decisions cannot be inferred solely from being the grandmother or kinship caregiver.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Role and authority language.","grader_hint":"Look for a prompt to clarify the recognized educational decision-maker or participation role rather than an assertion that Noor holds legal authority."},{"rubric_item_id":"R40","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The brief gives Noor a respectful way to ask who can consent, sign, or receive formal notices if that issue arises.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Procedural question.","grader_hint":"Award for a plain-language clarification question that does not purport to decide Noor's legal status."},{"rubric_item_id":"R41","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The brief does not tell Noor that she must sign immediately or that a signature necessarily means agreement.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Signature-related language.","grader_hint":"Review any signing prompt for neutral, non-jurisdiction-specific wording that encourages clarification before signing."},{"rubric_item_id":"R42","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The brief gives Noor usable language to request that each material proposal, refusal, or unresolved issue be clearly documented.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Decision-record script.","grader_hint":"Look for a speakable request covering what was agreed, declined, or left open rather than a generic instruction to take notes."},{"rubric_item_id":"R43","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The brief gives Noor a neutral way to ask for the team's reasons and supporting information when a request is declined.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Refusal-response script.","grader_hint":"The wording should seek the basis for the decision without alleging misconduct or predetermination."},{"rubric_item_id":"R44","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The brief avoids asserting a procedural violation merely because the team disagrees with Noor or declines a requested support.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Legal and procedural language.","grader_hint":"Confirm the page distinguishes disagreement from a proven violation and contains no unsupported accusation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R45","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The brief prompts Noor to confirm what will begin now under the existing or agreed plan rather than waiting indefinitely for perfect information.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Immediate-action question.","grader_hint":"Look for a practical question about current implementation that does not presume a particular service must be adopted."},{"rubric_item_id":"R46","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The brief separately prompts for further assessment or review when current information is insufficient to define the reading need.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Assessment-related question.","grader_hint":"Award when additional evaluation is framed as something to consider or formally decide, not as proof of eligibility."},{"rubric_item_id":"R47","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The brief does not claim that a request for assessment automatically establishes eligibility, a diagnosis, or a particular service.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Assessment and eligibility wording.","grader_hint":"Check that the page preserves the distinction between seeking information and predetermining the outcome."},{"rubric_item_id":"R48","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The brief asks how instructional and support continuity will be maintained despite the child's placement transitions.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Continuity question.","grader_hint":"Look for a concrete prompt about avoiding further gaps in implementation, records, materials, or communication."},{"rubric_item_id":"R49","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The brief requests a named role or clear point of contact for follow-up without inventing a person.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Follow-up prompt.","grader_hint":"Award when Noor is prompted to record who is responsible by name or role, but the document itself does not fabricate that information."},{"rubric_item_id":"R50","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The brief prompts for a concrete follow-up or review date without inventing one.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Follow-up prompt and note space.","grader_hint":"Look for a blank or question that causes the meeting to produce an actual date."},{"rubric_item_id":"R51","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The brief includes a concise end-of-meeting read-back or summary script covering decisions, responsibilities, and timing.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Closing script.","grader_hint":"The closing should help Noor verify shared understanding before the meeting ends."},{"rubric_item_id":"R52","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The brief prompts Noor to ask for a copy of the resulting plan or meeting record in a form she can review.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Closing or records request.","grader_hint":"Accept a plain request for the completed or revised document; do not require jurisdiction-specific timing language."},{"rubric_item_id":"R53","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document limits disclosure of child-welfare history to educationally relevant context and does not encourage sharing the full case record.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Historical script and any records guidance.","grader_hint":"Confirm that the two moves and interrupted instruction are the extent of child-welfare detail and that the page does not direct Noor to hand over the CCWIS export or provider reports."},{"rubric_item_id":"R54","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document contains no invented scores, dates, service minutes, attendance totals, legal status, or prior school responses.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"All case-specific assertions in the brief.","grader_hint":"Compare every case-specific number or factual claim with the limited facts in the request; generic blanks or questions are acceptable."},{"rubric_item_id":"R55","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document contains no legal citations, case citations, statutory section numbers, or agency-system instructions.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Full document text.","grader_hint":"Confirm the page remains a caregiver aid rather than a legal memorandum or CCWIS procedure."},{"rubric_item_id":"R56","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The brief uses plain language or immediately explains any unavoidable IEP terminology.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Vocabulary throughout.","grader_hint":"A caregiver should not need to know professional acronyms or technical reading terminology to use the page."},{"rubric_item_id":"R57","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The tone is calm, collaborative, and firm enough to support advocacy without sounding accusatory or apologetic.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Speaking scripts and questions.","grader_hint":"Assess whether Noor could use the language with a school team while preserving both clarity and working relationships."},{"rubric_item_id":"R58","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Prompts are concise and genuinely speakable rather than explanatory paragraphs written for a professional reader.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Length and construction of scripts and questions.","grader_hint":"Most prompts should be usable aloud with little or no editing by Noor."},{"rubric_item_id":"R59","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The page differentiates items Noor needs the meeting to resolve from optional or desirable requests she should raise.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Labels, wording, or hierarchy of prompts.","grader_hint":"Look for a clear must/should boundary: core clarification and documentation are not conflated with a guarantee that every preferred support will be adopted."},{"rubric_item_id":"R60","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Noor could independently use the brief to open the meeting, provide the relevant context, ask for defensible decisions, capture answers, and close with confirmed next commitments.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"The complete rendered artifact.","grader_hint":"Judge the page as an operational tool for a caregiver attending alone; it should not require Noor to ask the author what a prompt means or what to do next."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"A government child and family social worker is preparing a constituent-facing advocacy aid for a kinship caregiver attending an IEP meeting alone. The brief must compress limited case context into accurate, usable meeting language without overstating rights, evidence, or likely outcomes.","difficulty_sources":["Selecting only educationally relevant context from a large underlying case while no source records are available to the author","Balancing immediate reading advocacy with accurate documentation of team decisions within one page","Explaining when placement history is educationally relevant without asserting causation","Distinguishing required clarification and documentation from supports that may be requested but are not guaranteed","Avoiding assumptions about diagnosis, caregiver authority, attendance, eligibility, and service dosage","Writing language a caregiver can actually say and annotate during a live meeting"],"authoring_plan":{"solver_instance":"A government child and family social worker must create a new, one-page caregiver-facing advocacy aid from occupational knowledge alone. The artifact must be usable during a live IEP meeting and must preserve doctrinal boundaries despite minimal case facts.","behaviour_specification":["Choose either immediate reading planning or accurate decision documentation as the primary frame, make that choice visually and rhetorically explicit, and retain the other as a secondary concern.","Use the two placement moves only to explain interrupted instructional continuity and why present data require careful interpretation.","Do not present placement disruption as the cause of a disability, diagnosis, or entitlement.","Redirect from old diagnostic wording to current educational performance, evidence, and needs.","Provide first-person scripts and direct questions that a caregiver can say without professional translation.","Separate current performance, goal setting, targeted instruction, access accommodations, progress monitoring, decision recording, and follow-up.","Seek implementable details for agreed supports while leaving all unsupported values blank or for the team to determine.","Clarify the caregiver's participation and possible authority without assuming legal decision-making status.","Maintain a firm distinction between matters the team should address or document and preferred supports that Noor may request but cannot treat as guaranteed.","End with a read-back that captures decisions, refusals or open items, responsibility, timing, and the record Noor will receive."],"doctrinal_pairs":[{"rule":"Relevant caregiver observations should be heard and considered.","must_not_claim":"Consideration requires adoption of every caregiver request."},{"rule":"Placement history may be relevant when it explains interrupted educational access or how present data should be interpreted.","must_not_claim":"Placement moves prove the cause of a disability or reading deficit."},{"rule":"Current reading performance should be described using recent, understandable evidence.","must_not_claim":"An unspecified older diagnosis establishes current performance, eligibility, or services."},{"rule":"Attendance information may inform interpretation.","must_not_claim":"Attendance alone explains, disproves, or resolves the reading need."},{"rule":"A measurable goal requires an established baseline and defined method of measurement.","must_not_claim":"The author can invent an appropriate baseline or target without data."},{"rule":"Access accommodations and skill-building instruction answer different needs.","must_not_claim":"An accommodation automatically substitutes for targeted reading instruction."},{"rule":"Agreed services need enough detail to be implementable.","must_not_claim":"A particular provider, frequency, setting, or service is guaranteed before the team decides."},{"rule":"Insufficient current information can justify asking the team to consider further assessment.","must_not_claim":"Requesting assessment automatically proves eligibility, diagnosis, or entitlement."},{"rule":"Material proposals, refusals, reasons, and open issues should be captured clearly.","must_not_claim":"A disagreement or refusal by itself proves a procedural violation."},{"rule":"A kinship caregiver can contribute relevant information and advocacy.","must_not_claim":"Grandparent or kinship-caregiver status alone proves authority to consent or make educational decisions."},{"rule":"A signer should understand what a document represents.","must_not_claim":"Noor must sign immediately or that every signature necessarily signifies agreement."},{"rule":"The meeting should identify what can be implemented now and what needs more information.","must_not_claim":"Either immediate support or further assessment must wait for the other in all cases."}],"wide_rule_of_thumb_tension":"The common instinct to omit placement history from a school meeting stops being sound when a tightly bounded account of placement changes is necessary to explain interrupted instruction or interpret educational data. The gold should include that context briefly and then return to present educational decisions.","must_should_boundary":"The gold must distinguish core matters that require clarification and documentation for a usable plan—current need, evidence, decisions, implementation responsibility, progress monitoring, and unresolved items—from supports Noor should request for team consideration but cannot label as predetermined entitlements. It must also distinguish Noor's right to meaningful participation from unverified authority to consent.","case_fact_constraints":["There were two prior placement moves.","Continuity of instruction was interrupted around those moves.","There is a widening reading gap.","Older diagnostic wording exists but is not identified and should not lead the meeting.","No other case-specific fact, number, diagnosis, date, attendance pattern, legal role, prior response, or service detail may be asserted."],"intended_verdict":"A passing reference solution is a single rendered page that Noor can scan, speak from, and annotate. It makes one defensible framing choice, handles placement history as limited educational context, uses current-evidence questions instead of diagnostic advocacy, draws the must/should boundary accurately, and avoids unsupported legal or case claims.","offline_validation":"Construct and render the DOCX with standard offline office tooling. Inspect page count, editable content, note space, all factual assertions, doctrinal pairings, speaking usability, and the consistency of the chosen primary frame. The imagined reference solution satisfies every rubric item without external research or hidden source material."},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"single_artifact","structure":"freeform"},"reference_files":[],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"iep_advocacy_brief","filename":"noor_aubert_iep_advocacy_brief.docx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","description":"A one-page, plain-language IEP advocacy brief that Noor Aubert can speak from and annotate during the meeting.","required":true,"constraints":["Exactly one editable DOCX file","No more than one rendered page","Written directly for Noor Aubert to use in the meeting","Includes usable speaking language, questions, and room for short notes","Uses only the case facts stated in the request","Does not name or infer a diagnosis or invent scores, dates, service minutes, attendance totals, legal status, or prior school responses","Contains no legal citations or agency-process instructions","Must be saved at the top level of the working directory as noor_aubert_iep_advocacy_brief.docx"],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"communicate_stakeholders","work_product":"operating_plan","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"closed_world_with_assumptions"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"authored_doc@v4","occupation":"child_family_school_social_workers","sector":"government","task_archetype":"authored_doc","estimated_professional_hours":2.5,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"domain_expert","reviewer_policy":"The reference solution should be reviewed by a child and family social-work practitioner familiar with school meetings and by an independent special-education practitioner for accuracy, caregiver usability, and restraint. Reviewers should accept either reading-plan-first or decision-record-first framing when the chosen priority is deliberate, internally consistent, and does not erase the secondary concern.","minimum_reviewers":2,"known_limitations":["No school records or jurisdiction-specific procedural documents are supplied, so the gold must not depend on local timelines, forms, eligibility categories, or signature rules.","The caregiver's formal educational decision-making status is unknown and must remain unresolved in the brief.","The limited facts do not support a diagnosis, quantified baseline, specific service dosage, attendance conclusion, or predetermined IEP outcome."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"成品包存在","detail":"按公开题面存在纳入抽样；不视为内容正确性验收。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T18:38:48+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T18:38:48+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T18:38:48+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T18:38:48+00:00"},{"check":"instruction_rubric_overlap","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":false,"required":false,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"instruction 与 rubric criterion 存在 8-gram 逐字重叠: ['R54']","checked_at":"2026-08-20T18:38:48+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_b1/runs/f5d7c768bb870561","declared_deliverables":["noor_aubert_iep_advocacy_brief.docx"]};
